Stephen: "my left and right are inverted in the abduct a chameleon 3D."

moveLocal() built its strafe axis as right = UP x fwd. The camera looks ALONG
fwd (orbit() parks it at c - fwd*dist and lookAt(c)), so the vector the player
actually sees on their right is fwd x UP — the exact opposite. Every strafe input
was mirrored: touch stick, keyboard A/D and the gamepad X axis alike. Forward and
back were always correct, which is why it read as "left and right are inverted"
rather than "the controls are broken".

flyLocal() (spectator free-fly) had it right the whole time — the two functions
disagreed, and the gameplay one was the wrong one.

Measured, not reasoned: an instrumented copy of the real game exposed localPos +
yaw, and the probe pushed the stick and read the world-space delta against the
true screen-right vector.
  before: stick RIGHT -> 4.5 units along screen-LEFT   (INVERTED)
          stick LEFT  -> 4.5 units along screen-RIGHT  (INVERTED)
          stick UP    -> forward                       (correct)
  after:  RIGHT -> screen-right, LEFT -> screen-left, UP -> forward (all correct)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 abduct-3d.html | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/abduct-3d.html b/abduct-3d.html
index e6ad6e4..19aa9a5 100644
--- a/abduct-3d.html
+++ b/abduct-3d.html
@@ -1830,7 +1830,11 @@ function clientTick(dt){
 
 function moveLocal(dt, role){
   const y = role==='seeker' ? seekerYaw : yaw;
-  fwd.set(Math.sin(y),0,Math.cos(y)); right.crossVectors(UP,fwd).normalize(); localYaw = y;
+  // right must be the vector the PLAYER sees on their right. The camera looks along
+  // fwd, so screen-right is fwd x UP. This was UP x fwd — the exact opposite — which
+  // mirrored strafing for touch, keyboard A/D and the gamepad alike ("my left and
+  // right are inverted"). flyLocal() below always had it the right way round.
+  fwd.set(Math.sin(y),0,Math.cos(y)); right.crossVectors(fwd,UP).normalize(); localYaw = y;
   const mv = _a.set(0,0,0);
   if(keys['KeyW']) mv.add(fwd); if(keys['KeyS']) mv.sub(fwd);
   if(keys['KeyD']) mv.add(right); if(keys['KeyA']) mv.sub(right);
